
(note BZ-RulesOfEngagement-01)
(time 240)

; Acceptance test for the weaponsHold rule in bravozero-extensions.kif.
;
; The JOSHUA ROE block (2026-03-04) states in its header comment:
;
;   "Step 0 inference (acceptance test):
;      Given (attribute ?AGENT weaponsHold) and (instance ?ATTACK Attack)
;      and (agent ?ATTACK ?AGENT), prove there exists a prior ViolentContest
;      where ?AGENT was the patient (self-defense justification)."
;
; That test was described in prose but never encoded in a runnable form.
; This file turns the description into a theorem-prover query so the
; property is CI-enforceable rather than aspirational.
;
; Test setup: JTF-A is a CognitiveAgent under the weaponsHold profile.
; It executes Attack A-1 against target T-1.  The weaponsHold rule
; should force the existence of a prior ViolentContest where T-1 was
; the aggressor against JTF-A.  If Vampire proves that existential,
; the rule does what its documentation claims.

(instance JTF-A CognitiveAgent)
(instance T-1 CognitiveAgent)
(instance A-1 Attack)

(attribute JTF-A weaponsHold)
(agent A-1 JTF-A)
(patient A-1 T-1)

(query
  (exists (?THREAT)
    (and
      (instance ?THREAT ViolentContest)
      (agent ?THREAT T-1)
      (patient ?THREAT JTF-A)
      (earlier (WhenFn ?THREAT) (WhenFn A-1)))))

(answer yes)
